<http://data.silknow.org/object/98949d94-c092-3020-aea0-1b0245dd525f/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Furnishing fabric of stamped plush velveteen. With an 18th century large-scale symmetrical pattern with flowers and larger leaves springing from a central stem, and stamped in two levels on a pink-tan silk pile. The material has a binding warp of pale blue cotton and double shots of pink cotton weft. Wide selvedges are woven with paired warp threads, 5 blue, 4 white and 8 blue. On the back of the material is printed in black ink with 'R.M. &amp; Co.' three times along one edge."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/98949d94-c092-3020-aea0-1b0245dd525f> .

